# Documentation Navigation Rules

This is a **pointer**, not the definition. This file used to say "Step 1: Read `CLAUDE.md` first —
it contains project overview and tech stack, critical rules, project structure" — stale (#365):
root `CLAUDE.md` is now a 4-line pointer (`@AGENTS.md`), and `AGENTS.md` is what's actually
auto-loaded and canonical.

**Read `AGENTS.md` in full and follow it first.** For its "Mandatory Documentation Lookup Order"
and doc-authority rules, don't duplicate them here — a second copy of the same navigation rule
independently drifting is exactly the staleness failure this file itself became an example of.

The general token-efficiency habit this file used to teach (read a large file's TOC/first section
before loading it whole, grep before scrolling) is still good practice — just apply it to whatever
`AGENTS.md`'s lookup order actually points you at, not to the specific file list that used to be
hardcoded here.
